From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ArchPad Project <archpad@localhost>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:12:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: q6v5: disable handover irq after handover

On Qualcomm SoCs such as SM8250, the Sensors Low-Power Island (SLPI) DSP
firmware toggles SMP2P handover status bits during runtime sensor sampling
and power state changes. Because the handover interrupt is not masked
after the initial boot handover handshake completes, each transition
re-enters q6v5_handover_interrupt and emits:
  "Handover signaled, but it already happened"
at up to 5 times per second, flooding dmesg and the system journal.

Disable the handover interrupt via disable_irq_nosync() immediately once
handover is processed. The interrupt is re-enabled in qcom_q6v5_prepare()
on the next remoteproc start. In qcom_q6v5_unprepare(), only disable the
interrupt if handover was not already completed to maintain balance.

Signed-off-by: ArchPad Project <archpad@localhost>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 24eb37452..68c4a5c37 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -81,7 +81,8 @@ int qcom_q6v5_prepare(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5)
  */
 int qcom_q6v5_unprepare(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5)
 {
-	disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
+	if (!q6v5->handover_issued)
+		disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
 	q6v5_load_state_toggle(q6v5, false);
 
 	/* Disable interconnect vote, in case handover never happened */
@@ -168,6 +169,8 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
+	disable_irq_nosync(q6v5->handover_irq);
+
 	if (q6v5->handover)
 		q6v5->handover(q6v5);
 
-- 
